Research notes for the implementer — these are notes to help, not a spec. Please still read the issue body and CLAUDE.md yourself and verify anything critical before making changes.

I re-verified the claims in the issue directly against the current code on master (no web research was needed here — this is a pure internal dead-code deletion, not a library/API question):

What to remove
- app/app/index.tsx lines 1751-1758, the `openBatterySettings` useCallback block:
  const openBatterySettings = useCallback(() => {
    if (Platform.OS !== "android") return;
    Linking.sendIntent("android.settings.IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATION_SETTINGS").catch(() => {
      Linking.sendIntent("android.settings.SETTINGS").catch(() => {
        Linking.openSettings().catch(() => {});
      });
    });
  }, []);

Confirmed unused
- `grep -rn "openBatterySettings" app tests website` returns only that one definition line — no call site, no prop pass-through, nothing in JSX.
- Its neighbors `openAppSettings` (line 1747-1749) and `openExactAlarmSettings` (line 1760-1765) ARE both wired into `AndroidBackgroundHelpModal` via `onOpenAppSettings` / `onOpenExactAlarmSettings` props (index.tsx around 2025-2026, and the modal's prop types/usage at app/components/AndroidBackgroundHelpModal.tsx lines 36/38/72/73/90/102). There is no `onOpenBatterySettings`-style prop on that modal, and no other component references it either.
- The modal's "Notifications, full-screen alarms & battery" step (AndroidBackgroundHelpModal.tsx, around lines 80-87) already tells the user in plain static text to go to Settings → Battery → set Cue Clock to "No restrictions"/"Unrestricted". That text does not depend on `openBatterySettings` at all, so deleting the function does not remove any user-facing guidance.

Safe to delete cleanly — no follow-on cleanup needed
- `Linking` and `Platform` (imported at the top of index.tsx) are both still used extensively elsewhere in the file (Linking.openSettings/sendIntent in the two sibling helpers, and Platform.OS is referenced ~36 times across the file), so removing this block will not orphan either import. No import-line edit is needed.
- Just delete the 8-line block; nothing else in the file references it, so no other edits should be required.

Verification the implementer should do afterward (matches what the issue itself asks for)
- Run `npx tsc --noEmit` inside `app/` to confirm no dangling reference/type error.
- If possible, exercise the real onboarding flow: the Android-only `AndroidBackgroundHelpModal` first-launch wizard step titled "Notifications, full-screen alarms & battery" should still render its instructional text, and its "App settings" and "Exact alarm settings" buttons (backed by `openAppSettings`/`openExactAlarmSettings`) should still work exactly as before. This step is Android-only per CLAUDE.md ("iOS/web skip step 1"), so it can't be exercised on iOS/web — a Contributor without an Android device/emulator should say so rather than claim it was tested.

CLAUDE.md considerations
- This is a plain deletion of genuinely dead code with zero behavior change, which fits the "MUST stay minimal" non-negotiable and touches nothing related to timing, alarms, the 3-second beep, or notification/alarm scheduling (none of which call this function).
- No comment-style concerns apply since the whole block is being removed, not edited into something needing a new comment.
- This is not a CI/workflow file change, so the "claude-" prefix workflow-naming rule and the release-trigger invariants don't apply here.

I could not find anything that contradicts the issue's proposal; the removal appears exactly as safe and scoped as described.
